<header><h1>The Fracture: Proof</h1></header>
<article>
<p>The source text behind each note on <a href="/R_fracture">The Fracture</a>. <b>Explicit</b> sources state the note directly. <b>Implicit</b> sources support it without stating it.</p>

<h2>Notes</h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Fracture consists of additional systems beyond the regular bounds of the game map.<sup>7</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Rulebook p. 9, The Fracture: &ldquo;The Fracture is an enigmatic area of space that is not connected to the rest of the galaxy.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When a player gains their breakthrough, they roll a dice. On a result of 1 or 10, The Fracture enters play. Other game effects may also bring The Fracture into play.<sup>7</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> Thunder&rsquo;s Edge reference: &ldquo;Roll a die on gaining breakthrough; on a roll of 1 or 10, that player puts The Fracture into play.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> p. 9 mentions Fracture &ldquo;brought into play by another ability.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>The &ldquo;0&rdquo; side of the d10 represents a result of 10.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Yes, the &lsquo;0&rsquo; face is a &lsquo;10&rsquo; result.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Does the 0 on the ten-sided die count as 0 or 10?&rdquo;: &ldquo;10.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>When The Fracture enters play, it is placed against the edge of the regular game map.<sup>7</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Rulebook p. 9, The Fracture: &ldquo;the player that brought it into play places it along any edge of the game board, based on player count.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>The placement location of The Fracture is arbitrary, and should have no mechanical effect on the game state.<sup>2,7</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Rulebook p. 9, The Fracture: &ldquo;Regardless of where The Fracture is placed, its systems are not adjacent to the systems it is touching.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Is The Fracture 3 systems or 7 &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;It can sit anywhere, and the galaxy tiles it touches stay edge systems.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>All systems in The Fracture are considered to be on the edge of the game board.<sup>2,7</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Rulebook p. 9, The Fracture: &ldquo;each of its systems is considered to be on the edge of the game board.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal: &ldquo;every Fracture system also counts as on the edge.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>While The Fracture is not in play, its systems, such as the one containing Styx, are not legal targets for abilities such as those of the <a href="/F_yin">Yin</a> player&rsquo;s and <a href="/F_lizix">L1Z1X</a> player&rsquo;s heroes.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;Can the Yin or L1Z1X hero be used on Styx if the Fracture isn&rsquo;t in Play? A: No. The Fracture is not in play and not a legal target.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If The Fracture enters play as a result of the expedition that also places <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Thunder&#x27;s_Edge">Thunder&rsquo;s Edge</a>, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Thunder&#x27;s_Edge">Thunder&rsquo;s Edge</a> is placed first, and then the final ingress token is placed in its system.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;Thunder&rsquo;s Edge is placed, then you place the final Ingress in the Thunder&rsquo;s Edge system.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Attachments, such as the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Relics#Codex_II:~:text=Nano-Forge"><i>Nano&ndash;Forge</i></a> relic and the <a href="/F_ul">Ul</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Titans_of_Ul#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=Terraform"><i>Terraform</i></a> promissory note, may be attached to planets in The Fracture.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus, &ldquo;Can Nano-Forge and/or Terraform be attached to planets in The Fracture?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Can Nano-Forge and/or Terraform be attached to planets in The Fracture? A: Yes&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    <li>When The Fracture is brought into play, neutral units are placed on the planets in The Fracture as well as the space area of those planets&rsquo; systems, as indicated on the reverse side of The Fracture tiles.<sup>7</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Rulebook p. 9, The Fracture: &ldquo;They then place neutral units as indicated on the back of The Fracture&rsquo;s tiles.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When The Fracture is brought into play, several ingress tokens will be placed on the game board. Several systems in The Fracture contain a printed egress. Each ingress is adjacent to each egress, and vice versa. An ingress is not adjacent to an ingress and an egress is not adjacent to an egress.<sup>2,7</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Rulebook p. 9, The Fracture: &ldquo;A system that contains an ingress is adjacent to each system in The Fracture that contains an egress. However, ingress systems are not adjacent to other ingress systems, and egress systems are not adjacent to other egress systems.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can ships move from an egress back to an ingress to leave The Fracture?&rdquo;: &ldquo;ingress and egress adjacency works both ways, like wormholes, except ingresses aren&rsquo;t adjacent to other ingresses and egresses aren&rsquo;t adjacent to other egresses&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>With sufficient movement, a ship could move from a system containing an ingress in the regular game map, into a system containing an egress within The Fracture, and then out to a different system containing an ingress in the regular game map. A ship could also do the reverse to travel from an egress to a different egress via an ingress.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can ships pass through the Fracture in one move &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes, they can go in through one ingress and out via an egress to another ingress system if their move allows.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>If The Fracture was brought into play as a result of a player rolling a dice upon gaining their breakthrough, they will place ingress tokens according to the synergy on their breakthrough. For each color of technology in their breakthrough&rsquo;s synergy, they choose three planets with a matching technology specialty, and place an ingress token in that planet&rsquo;s system.<sup>7</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Rulebook p. 9, The Fracture: &ldquo;For each synergy color on their breakthrough, that player must choose three systems that contain matching technology specialties, if able, and place ingress tokens in those systems.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>If there are fewer than three planets with a technology specialty of a given color, as many planets as possible are chosen.<sup>7</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Rulebook p. 9, The Fracture: &ldquo;must choose three systems &hellip; if able.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>If a different game effect places The Fracture into play, or The Fracture enters play because of the <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player&rsquo;s breakthrough (which does not have a synergy), then the player that caused The Fracture to enter play chooses one planet with a technology specialty for each of the four colors of technology, and places ingress tokens in each of those planets&rsquo; systems.<sup>2,7</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Rulebook p. 9, The Fracture: &ldquo;If The Fracture was brought into play by another ability, or by a breakthrough that does not have synergy (as is the case with the Nekro Virus faction), the player chooses four planets and places an ingress token in those planets&rsquo; systems.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Who places ingress tokens when Rapid Mobilization brings the Fracture in?&rdquo;: &ldquo;the triggering player places ingress tokens in four different systems, each with a planet of a different specialty if able&rdquo; About Rapid Mobilization; Nekro not named.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If one system contains two planets with a technology specialty, only one of those planets may be chosen when placing ingress tokens.<sup>7</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Rulebook p. 9, The Fracture: &ldquo;Each planet must be in a different system and must have a different technology specialty.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>After ingress tokens are placed with either of these two methods, one additional ingress token is placed. If <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Thunder&#x27;s_Edge">Thunder&rsquo;s Edge</a> is on the game board, then an ingress token is place into its system. Otherwise, an ingress token is placed into the <a href="/R_mecatol_rex">Mecatol Rex</a> system.<sup>7</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Rulebook p. 9, The Fracture: &ldquo;Finally, the players place an ingress token in the Thunder&rsquo;s Edge system, if it is in play, or in the Mecatol Rex system, if the expedition has not been completed.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A system cannot contain two or more ingress tokens.<sup>6,7</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Rulebook p. 9, The Fracture: &ldquo;A system cannot have more than one ingress token.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;the rules state that a system may not contain more than 1 ingress token.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>When a player gains control of a planet in The Fracture that is not already controlled by another player, they draw one relic card.<sup>7</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Rulebook p. 9: &ldquo;Each planet in the fracture has a relic icon.&rdquo; p. 10: &ldquo;When a player gains a planet card from the planet deck that has a relic icon &hellip; they draw the top card of the relic deck.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
</article>
